# Linear Equations

## What I learned
Linear equations allow you to find
the value of an unknown.

Key Rules
No exponents: Variables are never squared (\[x^{2}\]), cubed (\[x^{3}\]), or raised to other powers.
No multiplication of variables: Terms never multiply variables together (like \[xy\]).
No roots or denominators: Variables do not appear inside square roots, cube roots, or fractions in the denominator (\[\frac{1}{x}\]). 

## Example

2x + 4 = 12

2x = 12 - 4

2x = 8

x = 4

## Practice

